          "text": "8.2 The Light-Dependent Reactions of\nPhotosynthesis\nLearning Objectives\nBy the end of this section, you will be able to do the following:\nExplain how plants absorb energy from sunlight\nDescribe short and long wavelengths of light\nDescribe how and where photosynthesis takes place within a plant\nHow can light energy be used to make food? When a person turns on a lamp, electrical energy\nbecomes light energy. Like all other forms of kinetic energy, light can travel, change form, and be\nharnessed to do work. In the case of photosynthesis, light energy is converted into chemical energy,\nwhich photoautotrophs use to build basic carbohydrate molecules (Figure 8.9).",
